# Always push after every change

When the user asks you to make a change (fix, feature, config, assets, etc.):

1. **Implement** the change
2. **Commit** with a clear message on a `cursor/<descriptive-name>-8262` branch
3. **Push** to origin immediately: `git push -u origin <branch-name>`
4. Only then tell the user the work is done

Never leave changes only local or uncommitted. Never say "done" without a successful push.

If push fails, retry with exponential backoff (4s, 8s, 16s, 32s) up to 4 times, then report the failure.

When multiple changes stack, merge PRs to `main` when the user asks to ship or merge.
